"## Summary\n\nPublishes the #478–#481 handover cut at b921c75f. It records isolation's planning/reviewer repair and members' fresh serving reads, archives review r32, and routes the six Node test failures and clone receiver wiring gap to their owners. Historical failed runs retain their verdicts.\n\nThe corrections repair D-162 source descriptions and evidence citations. Historical source claims now verify the pinned frozen inputs without requiring later product sources to remain identical. Independent review recomputed the 23 snapshots, 22 source readings, 22 declarations, 62 artifacts, 122 JSON values and preservation of 41 earlier claims. Scope is 52 owned files. The 241 digest changes are disclosed as 238 updates plus three stale pins for an unchanged index.\n\nD-150–D-163 were confirmed by the owner after this cutoff; their public confirmation update is assigned to handover 49. The authorized upstream comment likewise belongs to that later cut.\n\n## Orchestrator validation\n\nFinal delivery head is e221cf24479c9cd99eb87cbf14c454cd19fb5c1b. The integration check first exposed the frozen-source/current-source equality dependency; the narrow correction removes that equality and refreshes two scope digests while preserving all historical assertions and pinned evidence.\n\nUnder the orchestrator's reserved window, all checks passed on current main 729f914254211509c838f2efe73d3e8936bcf7e0 (including devstack 37 / #482) plus this branch, tree f6b4849b7dc548f64ddf01daa29f07dac7d5071a: handover-verify; uncached follow-up 47/48 claims (17 and 16 subtests); the complete handover package; secops tests; committed-evidence checks across netlab/e2e; root go-lint; tracked Go formatting; and diff check. Verification used disk scratch and its own temporary database, which was removed afterward.\n\nThis is a documentation/evidence delivery. The lane ran no Docker or live acceptance; the orchestrator's independent verification used the shared test database service only for its isolated database.\n\n## Lane delivery\n\n## Summary\n\nDelivered the `#478–#481` handover cut at `main` `b921c75f180beb6c0051d585a86d6651b2c8d71a` (`2026-11-04 EST`). Previous cut follow-up 47 (`#479`, merge `8a50c36c84628cce8b7c56e02d9123165d03ce84`, roadmap row `8f4374d3a6932d845317c994d6cd3de634cde37c`) remains the `#474–#477` cut at `1c39a0e73825dbcf911dfd2bec6e75aed64c979b` (`17` subtests / `4` roadmap rows / `4` PR excerpts / `13` byte-identical frozen inputs / `20` `main` Go test declarations / `20` frozen source readings / `92` archived artifacts / `38` exact JSON values / `40` earlier claims functions / `66` decisions / `136` findings rows / `238` secops digest changes; session `11:32–11:55 EST`, `9` commits and `45` owned files, `+12,104/−309`). No live acceptance was run by handover.\n\n`TestHandover_Followup48Claims`: **16 subtests / 4 exact roadmap rows / 4 PR body excerpts / 23 immutable snapshots / 22 `main` test declarations / 22 frozen source readings / 62 archived evidence artifacts / 122 exact JSON values without float conversion / 41 earlier claims functions preserved / 66 decisions (`2` updated, `0` added) / 138 findings (`6` updated, `2` added, `130` unchanged)**. `origin/r32-dedup-records-review:.agent/REVIEW.md` is archived byte-for-byte as `docs/reviews/r32-dedup-records-review.md` (`201` lines, `31,981` bytes, SHA-256 `5b7ec63eecbe64e278e16bf24ef3a8e9ea3e625d6bde701d6d0c0e5735e1960f` from `21e59029934a34f7125805e116a2ffaaf61b60cb`, base `1c39a0e73825dbcf911dfd2bec6e75aed64c979b`, committer `Ted H`, reviewer `agy/gemini-4-argon-high`, `0` Critical / `0` High / `0` Medium / `0` Low findings, `0` owner questions, `0` routed actions, with unmerged companion proof `node/agent/review_r32_test.go` frozen at `20,346` bytes / SHA-256 `8625fecccc518a49c10551bbd63d26be2807dc60b558816855182cb5d7ad999a` and `present_on_main = false`). Seven entrypoints (`README.md`, `docs/handover/00-index.md`, `docs/handover/deploy.md`, `docs/handover/member-guide.md`, `docs/handover/restore-drill.md`, `docs/handover/operator-guide.md`, `docs/ops/README.md`) are current. The scope inventory changes `241` SHA-256 values across `11` referenced paths: `238` owned-path updates across `10` paths, plus `3` repairs of stale pins for the unchanged `docs/e2e/at/secops/history/index.json`. No scope structure changes.\n\n**Running at briefing, status only:** `w2-agent-core` follow-up 53 (for the Node workflow's `node/agent` test failures across runs `41782791081`, `41787173794`, `41794009264`, `41808885873`, `41871089749` and `41885624816`, with the sixth added by the orchestrator, plus `F17-01`'s and `F31-01`'s design notes). No delivered or merged PR at the initial check; later results are after the cutoff and do not enter this cut.\n\nThe frozen-source claim now validates the pinned cutoff records without requiring current product files to retain historical bytes. Only that f48 condition/comment and the two handover-test SHA scalars changed in this correction; frozen inputs, predicate tokens, earlier claims and restoration checks are unchanged. The failed root combined run and verification status are recorded below.\n\n## Requirement and AT coverage\n\n- **§19 AT10–AT13 (`ISO01`–`ISO04`, `DNS03`, `ENT02`, `SEC01`), D-104 / D-140 / D-142 / D-161 / D-163 (`#478`, isolation follow-up 25, merge `014b59ab15288dc6bc053932104e26a8f3327e9e`, roadmap row `df61fd68add1678729ef32ae1ef93719124035e3`):** Archived 213-file failed follow-up 24 run `df9dbad7-049d-4eaa-ab98-5490906cc3e9` (measured source `56d814113913ddc6177d47d4a5160a65c93add25`) under `docs/e2e/at/isolation/history/follow-up-24/` (`archive.json`, SHA-256 `4dc62ef8d4af84cb97ffd1cfb73e230eefda29b0b6015ec36d5dc0977fb19157`, `37,721` bytes). Diagnosed `Isolation F24-01` under D-141 (`docs/e2e/at/isolation/history/follow-up-25-diagnosis/diagnosis.json`): calibration `latency_min_ns = \"122690\"`, `latency_median_ns = \"786977\"`, `latency_max_ns = \"2796647\"`, `latency_spread_ns = \"267395